Issue:
User reports inability to access a shared network folder that was previously accessible. Issue began unexpectedly without user-side configuration changes.

Environment:

Windows domain environment
Network shared drive (mapped and UNC access supported)
Standard user workstation

Troubleshooting Steps Taken:

Confirmed issue is isolated to shared network resource
Verified general network connectivity using external and internal ping tests
Checked access method (mapped drive / UNC path) for validity
Investigated potential permission or group membership changes
Verified accessibility of network share from alternate endpoints (if applicable)
Identified potential access control or group policy-related restriction

Root Cause:
Access likely affected due to permission changes, group membership modification, or mapping configuration issue.

Resolution:

Restored access by verifying correct group membership and permissions
Re-established network drive mapping (if applicable)
Confirmed user regained access to shared resource
Validated successful access with user

Tools Used:

Network connectivity tools (ping)
File share access via UNC path
User/group permission review (Active Directory concept)
Network drive mapping utilities
